# Browser verification — duplicate join conflict (Fix 1)

Date: 2026-10-22. App: http://localhost:3000 (dev, local Supabase + Midtrans sandbox).
Account: umkm3@gmail.com (test-only).

## 1. Real API contract (no mock)

POST /api/registrations  body: {"batchId":"e04707c7-0f6b-4f4c-bdc8-538bacc82c1d","quantity":1,"consentAccepted":true,"consentSnapshot":{"accepted":true}}
→ HTTP 409

{
  "error": "Anda sudah terdaftar pada batch ini.",
  "code": "REGISTRATION_ALREADY_EXISTS",
  "details": {
    "registrationId": "5c90d7bd-76c3-4dd6-ae55-e46b72304362",
    "quantity": 1,
    "canWithdraw": true
  }
}

Note: quantity 1 came from the request; the stored registration quantity is 30
(see the panel text below). `canWithdraw` is computed live by join_batch_v2.

## 2. Conflict panel (409 intercepted to reach the panel for an open batch)

Batch 1fd8e6b0-529a-425a-b1fd-29504bd33243, mocked 409 with quantity 2:

Anda sudah terdaftar pada batch ini.
Pendaftaran aktif tercatat dengan jumlah 2 pcs. Batalkan pendaftaran ini lebih dulu untuk memakai jumlah baru.
[link] Buka pesanan saya → /umkm/pesanan/5c90d7bd-76c3-4dd6-ae55-e46b72304362
Primary button: "Batalkan & daftar ulang" (enabled=true, bg-wesup-ink)

Screenshot: conflict-panel.png

## 3. Withdraw-and-rejoin (real API, mock removed before the click)

POST /api/umkm/orders/5c90d7bd-76c3-4dd6-ae55-e46b72304362/withdraw → 200 OK
POST /api/registrations → real request (route handler unregistered first); the
client navigated to the newly created order, so the re-join succeeded.
Result: /umkm/pesanan/f3c215d1-5535-4f08-ae23-aae90337f730 — order for batch
1fd8e6b0, quantity 1 — rendered with the payment countdown.

